# Vibesomnia engineering session log
# Append one dated entry per development session. No inferred hours, private
# machine details, chat contents, or fabricated verification. Runtime sessions
# are separate from this source-controlled development history.

2026-11-07 | Session 001 | Bootstrap v0.1.0-alpha.1
Objective: Start a working, fully open-source macOS alpha with accurate project
  documentation and version history. Defer Community/Pro editions.
Changes:
  - Added SwiftPM core, SwiftUI dashboard/menu/settings, native power service,
    optional Amphetamine automation, battery guard, AI app launch service, and CLI.
  - Added same-user bounded/expiring command transport; no network listener.
  - Added build/run bundle script, Codex Run action, tests, and CI definition.
  - Added README, AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, CHANGELOG.md, VERSION,
    roadmap, test checklist, and this engineering log.
Verification:
  - swift test: 8 tests passed (timer boundaries, app lifetime, validation,
    request expiry, launch allowlist, private file transport, stale status,
    symlink rejection).
  - Build/run --verify: app bundle launched and CLI responded.
  - Live native assertions: system-only and system+display modes acquired the
    expected assertions; stop and toggle released them.
  - Real one-minute timeout completed in the dashboard and released assertions.
  - Disposable GUI fixture exit ended its app-lifetime session and released power.
  - CLI launched the installed Codex GUI app successfully.
  - Dashboard, running/off states, countdown, app choices, and battery settings
    inspected through computer use; no visual overlap observed at default size.
  - Added and passed repeatable runtime smoke test for native controls and quit.
  - Fixed a shutdown stall found by smoke testing: AppKit termination now returns
    to the normal run loop before async cleanup, then terminates explicitly.
  - git diff --check passed; generated builds and private logs are ignored.
Limitations: Full Amphetamine parity, independent closed-lid support, full remote
  desktop control, persistent preferences, notarization, and physical lid tests
  are not complete. App-store feasibility and monetization are backlogged.
Next: Owner review of the running alpha; opt-in closed-lid/charger hardware tests,
  independent remote SSH testing, richer triggers, and native closed-lid design.
Delivery: Feature branch feat/v0.1.0-alpha.1; version 0.1.0-alpha.1. No binary
  release, notarization, app-store submission, or default-branch merge in this session.

2026-11-07 | Session 002 | App icon · v0.1.0-alpha.2
Objective: Create an app-related icon with a bloodshot-eyed developer vibe coding.
Changes:
  - Created a late-night developer mascot with messy hair, bloodshot eyes, dark
    hoodie, laptop, and lavender screen glow using the built-in image tool.
  - Added original artwork, PNG, ICNS, provenance/prompt, and repeatable exports.
  - Wired the icon into the macOS bundle, dashboard, and README.
  - Advanced alpha version strings and changelog to 0.1.0-alpha.2.
Verification:
  - swift test: all 8 tests passed.
  - Build/run --verify: alpha.2 app launched and CLI responded.
  - ICNS decoded successfully; 16px and 1024px family dimensions verified.
  - PNG is 1024x1024 with alpha; bundled ICNS matches the checked-in asset.
  - Ad-hoc app signature verified.
  - Computer-use screenshot confirmed the mascot appears in the dashboard.
  - Explicit bundled icon loading corrected a cached generic-icon preview.
Delivery: Feature branch feat/app-icon; source version v0.1.0-alpha.2.
Limitations: The detailed mascot is intended for app/Dock branding; the menu bar
  continues using native monochrome status symbols. No power behavior changed.
